---
description: Kloxo CP project rules (always apply)
alwaysApply: true
---

Before any work, read `docs/HANDOFF_BRIEFING.md` and `AGENTS.md`.

- Project: Kloxo CP, fork of Kloxo-MR, AGPLv3. Target Ubuntu 24.04, PHP 8.3, Nginx + PHP-FPM for sites,
  Hiawatha for the panel only, Postfix + Dovecot + Rspamd + MariaDB for mail, no billing, keep the UI.
- The legacy PHP under `kloxo/httpdocs` is PHP 5-era and UNSAFE. Do not run it on a public server.
  Fix security items P0 in the briefing before porting anything.
- Do not mass-rename `lx*` identifiers, DB columns, or the `lxlabs` account. Do not remove copyright notices.
- Never commit secrets or private keys. Generate keys at install time.
- New PHP: `declare(strict_types=1)`, PDO prepared statements, argument-array process execution (never shell
  strings), validate all input, add tests next to the change.
- Service configuration is generated from templates (`kloxo/file/mail/` is the model): render, validate with
  the service's own checker, install atomically, roll back on failure. Never edit generated files by hand.
- Mail design invariants (do not regress): TLS required for logins; Argon2id hashes; sender must match the
  authenticated login; unknown recipients rejected during SMTP; quota check before `permit_mynetworks`;
  catch-all must not swallow real mailboxes; `milter_default_action = tempfail`; DKIM via generated maps;
  flush Dovecot auth cache on account changes.
- Prefer deleting dead code (Apache, Lighttpd, Varnish, Squid, ATS, qmail, ezmlm, billing) over porting it.
- Never claim a thing works without running it; state what was and was not tested.
